{
  "number": 34,
  "title": "Mentura: frame agents, training pipeline design and own-harness idea",
  "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"tchjhnsn\"} -->\n_Requested by **Torian** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01TRojivaFzywKqAKrsycdv8?thread=cmsg_01TRojivaFzywKqAKrsycdv81vDy1VKeKfWw3ZBzrRwUwy)_\n\nConfidential Mentura work. All of it sits under `platform/`, so it moves with Mentura when Mentura splits into its own private repository after the demo (Torian's decision, 2026-10-29).\n\n## Frame agents (`platform/agents/frames/`)\n`run.mjs` runs one decision frame against a founder's problem, in this order:\n1. **framer** (Claude): writes the goal, the hidden decisions and the premises.\n2. **premise attacker** (Claude): writes one Noul proposition per premise.\n3. **Jev**: judges each proposition. At or above 0.7 the premise holds; at or below 0.3 it fails.\n4. **scout**: does the freshness lookup. It uses Firecrawl, or the agent's web search when there is no Firecrawl key.\n5. **reframer** (Claude): classifies the problem as a false dichotomy, a trade-off or a sequence, and writes the reframed question and the decisions.\n6. **code**: writes open decision records drafted by agents. Every option cites a source the scout found, and no agent decides.\n\nThe run produces one trace span per step. Code checks go to LangSmith as feedback with `--upload`: frame_has_no_answer, premises_judged, jev_decisive, verdict_valid, options_cited and founder_decides.\n\nFrames are read through a single adapter (`readFrame`) until the library schema lands on #33. The fixtures are a constructed frame and a constructed founder, never a real venture, and the data model check ignores them.\n\nA live run on the constructed founder used real Claude and real Jev. It returned \"false-dichotomy\", 8 propositions judged, 3 decision records and 12 cited sources, and every check scored 1 except jev_decisive, which scored 0.75.\n\n## Docs\n- `platform/design/agent-training-pipeline.md`: the agents, the split between Jev and code, the LangSmith loop, and the training signal (founder approvals now, outcomes later).\n- `platform/strategy/ideas/own-harness-home-field-2026-10-29.md`: an idea draft, not a record. It quotes Torian word for word.\n\n## Tests\n`node test.mjs` passes. It includes `platform/agents/frames/test.mjs`, which runs offline with a stand-in agent and a stand-in Jev.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01LJHEftA5fBfwCrWtkqnjkz",
  "headRefOid": "e6240aff349a4328fa1855e4c9b1fb7aaabe0544",
